## Context

Rung 3 of the ladder (`plugins/sdt-sitter/TESTING.md`, ruling 2026-09-23). The
author folded lifecycle testing into this rung rather than keeping it as a
layer, and merged "full Menagerie" with "wild documents": the corpus is where
the wild beasts belong. It is not to be called "acceptance": acceptance is the
author's own use (rung 5).

Today `bench/sitter_acceptance.py` runs its nine steps on four documents.

## Actions

1. Run the scenario over the whole Menagerie package (114 attachments today),
   so pause lands mid-document on a long book, not only before the first one.
2. Add to the scenario: replace the add-on under a running extraction, disable
   and re-enable, restart Zotero, then verify the census resumes and nothing is
   lost or duplicated.
3. Every eligible attachment ends with a pack or a named reason in the record.
4. Rename the driver and its record directory away from "acceptance", in one
   sweep with every reference.

## Test

Each new step first shown red on a payload built to fail it.

## Exit criteria

A recorded pass on the whole Menagerie with the integrity check (0816) green.
Once 0794 lands, the pass includes its two documents.
